Note the `agents/` <-> `orchestration/` cycle: agent protocol types currently live in `orchestration/round_table.py`, so `agents/` imports them back. It is a known wart -- tracked debt encoded as-is in `SRC_ALLOWED_IMPORTS`, documented rather than hidden.

**Two scopes, one wart.** The layer directories above (`{{ layers }}`) live at the project root and are *not* part of the installed package: `pip install -e .` installs only `src/{{ project_slug }}/`. Code inside the layers can import the package (`from {{ project_slug }}.llm import ...`), but the package never imports the layers, and the layers are importable only when running from the project root (pytest and the Makefile both do). This src-layout split is a known wart, documented rather than restructured.

