### Learning System (`learning/`)
- `models.py` -- `FeedbackSignal`, `UserPreference`, `AgentTrustScore`, `CheckIn`
- `schema.py` -- SQLite schema (4 tables, 6 indexes)
- `feedback_tracker.py` -- Record and query accept/reject/modify signals
- `agent_trust.py` -- EMA-based trust scoring per agent
- `checkin_manager.py` -- Permission-based adaptation (never adapts silently)
- `user_profile.py` -- Aggregates preferences + trust into context bundles
- `global_profile.py` -- Cross-project identity at `~/.aiscaffold/`
- `graduation.py` -- Rule engine proposing stable patterns for global promotion (pluggable rules, check-in gated; exposed at `/api/v1/graduation/*`)
- `store.py` -- Pluggable `LearningStore` protocol (6 methods) with SQLite (default) and Postgres reference backends (`LEARNING_BACKEND`); table definitions in `tables.py`
- `corrections.py` -- Correction lifecycle (proposed -> approved -> retired) with four-eyes approval and budgeted, sanitized prompt rendering
- `override_detector.py` -- Screens proposed corrections for injection, safety-agent targeting, and evidence-level inflation
- `collusion.py` -- Vote-lockstep, challenge-softness, and correction-drift detection over round-table history (tested detector library; the default runtime does not record votes into it -- see GOVERNANCE.md Non-Claims; correction drift gains an opt-in approve-path call site via `loop_integrity.py`)
- `loop_integrity.py` -- Opt-in, detect-only activation (`LOOP_INTEGRITY_DETECTION_ENABLED`, default off) for two formerly dormant detectors: correction drift (run on each corrections approval, cooldown-gated) and multi-turn poisoning (last-N-user-messages scan after each chat turn, session-keyed integrity flags). Activation/wiring only -- the detector implementations stay in `collusion.py` and `security/injection_defense.py`
- `activity.py` -- User activity thresholds (wired into the sampled activity middleware) and per-agent behavioral baselines over dispatch stats (baseline deviation checks are a library the default dispatch does not invoke -- see GOVERNANCE.md Non-Claims)
- `content_policy.py` -- Heuristic classifier for knowledge writes (approved/flagged/rejected); blocks standing-rule manipulation and persists integrity flags
- `reflector.py` -- Deterministic process-level lessons after each round table (agent effectiveness, evidence patterns, challenge impact, dissent value); capped, structured-fields-only, read via `GET /api/v1/reflections`
- `error_schemata.py` -- Generalizes clusters of approved corrections (>= 3, >= 2 distinct proposers) into reusable error schemas injected into single-shot context
- `contradiction.py` -- Pure-Python TF-IDF + negation heuristic flagging approved corrections that likely disagree; findings go to integrity flags
- `rag/` -- Vector store adapter, embeddings, semantic preference search. Search is truly semantic only with a real embedding provider (`EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=local|openai|auto`); the default hash fallback is deterministic filler whose vectors carry no meaning, so with the in-memory store retrieval then uses keyword matching instead of pretending cosine similarity works (Chroma has no keyword path -- hash vectors are stored as-is there, and ranking stays noise until a real provider is set)
- `rag/transcript_indexer.py` -- Indexes round table results for search over past deliberations (semantic with a real provider, keyword with the default fallback)
